<!--Post: 10992--><!--Time: 1110334500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10992"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 6:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was watching that on Crime TV last night. First off, was that new footage? The reason I ask is that it is pretty common knowlege around Wichita that the family living in the Otero&#39;s former house is making quite a point of keeping &#34;rubber neckers&#34; away. <BR> <BR>Second, the statement fits in with a recent pattern that points to the fact that the Information that has been released concerning the crime scene, particularly Joseph II, was not accurate. I re-read the letter from BTK concerning the Otero crime scene and it mentioned that he put 3 hoods on Joseph II: White t-shirt, white plastic bag, another t-shirt and his radio was blaring. <BR> <BR>The radio was blaring. Since BTK would want to hear someone entering the house, was the radio used to drown his screams. The t-shirts? Absorb blood, or sound, or because BTK was repulsed by the sight of what he &#40;or someone else had done&#41;? What happened to Joe junior that made him stick in that detective&#39;s mind more than a young girl hung half naked in the basement?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10992-->
<!--Post: 10994--><!--Time: 1110336891-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10994"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 6:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, <BR> <BR>My interpretation of this comment is different. Cops faced with death constantly become desensitized to differing degrees. Some never get over the sight of murder. Others compartmentalize ea murder by the severity of the crime scene. <BR> <BR>I believe this cop was either posturing by trying to look tough to his fellow officers, or he was trying not to give BTK the satisfaction &#40;BTK was seeking&#41;through shock value so he played it off, or maybe this guy is just one sick puppy ????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10994-->
<!--Post: 11003--><!--Time: 1110342632-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11003"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 8:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hbt, <BR> <BR>   LMAO <BR> <BR>Ember, <BR> <BR>   I want to be omitted too! <BR> <BR>Tac, <BR> <BR>   Absolutely, I think you pegged it. <BR> <BR>Skov, <BR> <BR>   Please forgive my fellow Kansan, this cop.  This is a Kansas regional English problem.  I also use this construction in speaking, but not in writing.  &#34;The only thing&#34; is being used in a form of intentional understatement &#40;somewhat rural&#41; to mean &#34;This thing so much that it is like it was the only thing&#34;.  It does not translate well to the written word.  When I listened to him, I knew he was OK.  Many times when people say this, they will have a very serious tone, or shake their head slowly.  He means that this really bothered him, far more than anything else.  But it is not the only thing - trust me.  Think of a cowboy saying it very slowly and seriously:  &#34;The only thing that bothered me about that boy was the gleam in his eyes and that smile that told me somethin&#39; weren&#39;t right.&#34;  You can bet money it wasn&#39;t the only thing - just the BIGGEST thing. <BR> <BR>He was already in trouble at that point.  I knew he was knee-deep in alligators when he got into that part about children being &#34;omitted&#34;.  Bureaucratic and horror don&#39;t mix well.  He tried to keep from sounding emotional and it ended up worse. <BR> <BR>This is why people like me are not allowed to talk to reporters.  I could have easily said the same thing he did.  That is why companies, governments, and police departments pay people with public speaking experience to do press conferences and make public statements, and keep yokels like me away from microphones.  These are fine cops - they probably cried when they took the kids to see E.T.  They were obviously very hurt by what they saw that day. <BR> <BR>Skov, I love the way you catch all these weirdnesses in my native tongue.  My wife is right - I&#39;m still a hick.  YEE-HAAAH!!!!  Proud to come from the state that most resembles a computer punch card!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11003-->
<!--Post: 11004--><!--Time: 1110343225-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11004"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 8:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe it&#39;s late or maybe I am tired but Pax did you say swiss cheese? No maybe I am just hungry ok I agree with all the above, as a career student I took a classes in report writing in college, know what we did? learned to say exactly what we mean. With nouns, verbs, you know stuff<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11004-->
