</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 8:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh forgot to say for Police report writing lol<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11005-->
<!--Post: 11014--><!--Time: 1110349856-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11014"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:crazyhorse4440@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lola<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lola<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 10:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with Pax. I don&#39;t think of that cop as hardened nor egotistical - just inadequate in his ability to project his thoughts. The Otero murders greatly affected him then and still does now.  Maybe it had been his job to remove Joey Otero&#39;s body on that terrible day? - Since Joey&#39;s murder sticks in his mind so well. Lighten up on the guy...afterall, he&#39;s a victim too. <BR>Peace <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11014-->
<!--Post: 11018--><!--Time: 1110350853-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11018"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 10:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The fact that &#34;the boy&#34; affected him more than &#34;the girl&#34; still seems unusual to me, unless there was something about his body that was not released. According to the official report, JoeII was basically in the same position as the parents and the first people on the scene would not have even seen his face. <BR> <BR>I have never seen an actual hanging, nor have I seen the dead body of a little girl, but Josephine was hanging, unhooded, bound, and half naked from a pipe. It seems to me that would be 100 times more horrifying to anyone than a young boy who was hooded.  <BR> <BR>Plus, according to the official report, three bodies were found laying down, all bound, all with bags over the head, one was hanging by the neck. It seems that, aside from the circumstances of Josephine&#39;s death, the body that would stand out in his mind would be the one that was left in a position different from the others.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11018-->
<!--Post: 11023--><!--Time: 1110366134-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11023"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Haytrader<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Haytrader<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 3:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A friend who lives in Wichita told me just last week that there was more to the Otero scene than has been reported. All he would say is &#34;you don&#39;t want to know&#34;. The guy that said this worked at Coleman when DDC was there. He also attended WSU in the same time frame as DDC. I asked him just what he meant and all he would say was it &#40;the Otero murder scene&#41; was  much more grusome than the public has ever been told about. I don&#39;t know where this guy got his info but he claimed to know. Maybe whatever he is referring to has somthing to do with the boy and that is why the cop said the boy effected him more.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11023-->
<!--Post: 11029--><!--Time: 1110375171-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11029"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 5:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just read a report that was dated the end of Feb, in which Jack Watkins describes the scene in the otero house that morning. In it he states that the boy was tied to a chair. The report in the link above has the cop saying that the boy was under the bed. Big difference!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11029-->
<!--Post: 11030--><!--Time: 1110377345-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11030"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 6:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kayjay, I noticed the discrepancy too. In-fact, I started a thread about it because I was looking for an accurate account. <BR> <BR>If anyone knows which version is correct, please post it. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/76/647.html?1110336483#POST10128" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/76/647.htm l?1110336483#POST10128</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11030-->
<!--Post: 11031--><!--Time: 1110380445-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hmmm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 7:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the cop had a son of his own or maybe he didn&#39;t spend as much time with Josephine&#39;s body.  We don&#39;t know, as a basement is dark &#40;wasn&#39;t the report that the police officer who found her almost ran into her?&#41;.  Maybe this officer just didn&#39;t get a good look at her.  Also, with Joseph being upstairs, he saw him first.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11031-->
<!--Post: 11040--><!--Time: 1110386615-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11040"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 8:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s right Haytrader! I can see why you all are upset about the comments the former investigator made, but you apparently didn&#39;t see an earlier interview with this gentlemen. He has clearly been affected by that crime scene in ways that none of us can even begin to comprehend. I sincerely do not believe he meant any disrespect towards any victim at that particluar crime scene.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11040-->
<!--Post: 11067--><!--Time: 1110408284-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11067"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 2:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sometimes newspapers misquote people or use a segment of a conversation. I&#39;ve been misquoted in newsprint myself.  <BR>The initial shock of seeing the first child victim may have had a larger impact on him since he may have never seen a brutally murdered child before and the first impression stayed with him longer.  <BR>As is printed in the article it indeed looks like an insensitive comment.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11067-->
<!--Post: 11069--><!--Time: 1110410448-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11069"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 3:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks to all for your responses and explanations. <BR> <BR>You are probably all right but I still cant understand how this cop could use a phrase like &#34;the only thing that bothered me&#34; <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11069-->
<!--Post: 11085--><!--Time: 1110420003-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11085"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 6:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ll play devil&#39;s advocate for a moment and say that I&#39;m not completely surprised by that officer&#39;s statement.  He could just be a street-hardened cop who&#39;s seen a lot of violence and death as part of his job, to the point of being somewhat desensitized to it.  It&#39;s not unusual for cops &#40;or medical personnel for that matter&#41; to get desensitized to dealing with dead adults, no matter what the cause of death may be, but they take it hard when they see children that have been killed.  Well, still kind of a strange thing for him to say.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11085-->
<!--Post: 11086--><!--Time: 1110421198-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11086"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 6:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, skov, for taking this kindly. <BR> <BR>As for myself, the only thing I know is that I&#39;m never, ever going to use sentences that begin with &#34;The only thing&#34;.  I shall omit my vocabulary from that usage. &#60;wink/&#62; <BR> <BR>New theory:  gag order is to prevent WPD from committing more linguistic atrocities.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11086-->
<!--Post: 11089--><!--Time: 1110422269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11089"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 6:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Audrey I agree! This poor man looked as though he had lead and incredible hard life, and I&#39;m almost sure in that first interview he did say that the child in the chair was the first victim he had seen in the house. Skov, honey don&#39;t take it so personally. I understand why you were offended though! BTW - I really admire your research skills and I get my tulip bulbs from Denmark, the best in the world! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11089-->
<!--Post: 11317--><!--Time: 1110583912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11317"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 3:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, <BR> <BR>Point well taken. The cop&#39;s choice of words is crass and rather heartless. But like email sometimes what people wish to express loses it&#39;s intent or &#34;tone&#34; in a faceless/expressionless written form.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11317-->
</table></td></tr></table>
